&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Global Structure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Deliveroo is now part of DoorDash, bringing together teams with even greater reach, scale, and ambition. Depending on your role, you may collaborate with teammates, systems, and leaders across DoorDash and Wolt. Together, we’re unlocking new possibilities as one global team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Unified Privacy Platform team’s mission is to earn the trust of every DoorDash user by upholding their right to privacy, consent, and transparency. We are building a common privacy foundation across DoorDash, Wolt, and Deliveroo so Consumers, Dashers, and Merchants can understand how their data is used, control their choices, and exercise their privacy rights through simple, consistent experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work is organized around three connected pillars: the Privacy Center, a unified user-facing destination for privacy controls and rights; the Unified Privacy Platform, which captures and enforces consent, policy, jurisdictional requirements, and privacy actions; and Privacy Operations and Intelligence, which gives Legal, Support, Privacy, and engineering operators the workflows, diagnostics, audit history, and automation needed to resolve privacy work safely and efficiently.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Together, these capabilities turn fragmented, one-off compliance work into reusable platform primitives that can support new products, brands, and emerging regulations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: London, UK. This is a hybrid role, with 3 days a week in the office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DoorDash is looking for an Engineering Manager to lead the Unified Privacy Platform team. You will lead a team of backend and platform engineers responsible for the next generation of privacy and consent infrastructure, including the Privacy Center, the User Consent Platform, privacy-policy decisioning, self-service data-rights experiences, and the operational tooling required to manage privacy cases at global scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Engineering Manager, you will own and execute a multi-year vision for privacy at DoorDash. You will balance legal and regulatory correctness, user trust, security, reliability, and developer velocity while building systems that work consistently across DoorDash, Wolt, and Deliveroo. You will be a strategic partner to Product, Legal, Security, Data Governance, Marketing and Communications, and engineering leadership, establishing clear ownership boundaries and turning complex privacy requirements into scalable, self-service capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and mentor a high-performing team of backend and platform engineers, fostering a culture of ownership, privacy by design, operational excellence, and thoughtful cross-functional partnership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the technical strategy across the Privacy Center, the Unified Privacy Platform, and Privacy Operations and Intelligence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the cross-brand User Consent Platform, including canonical consent state, policy and configuration management, consent SDKs, audit history, and consistent enforcement across products and jurisdictions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver simple, self-service experiences for consent and communication preferences, Right to be Forgotten (RTF), Right to Information (RTI), and Data Subject Access Requests (DSARs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn emerging privacy and regulatory requirements into standardized platform capabilities instead of one-off product implementations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the migration from fragmented legacy consent systems to a single source of truth across DoorDash, Wolt, and Deliveroo, while managing compatibility and safe deprecation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define clear contracts with data-governance fulfillment systems and downstream product and storage teams so privacy actions are traceable, retryable, auditable, and correctly reflected back to users and operators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide architectural guidance for distributed systems that manage sensitive user choices, policy evaluation, orchestration, secure data delivery, reporting, and immutable audit trails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with recruiting to build a diverse and inclusive team, attracting and retaining exceptional engineering talent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Need to Thrive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s, master’s, or doctoral degree in Computer Science or a related field, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in people management leading backend or platform teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of industry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience as an engineer or engineering leader in a fast-paced, platform-focused development environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience designing large-scale distributed systems, service application programming interfaces (APIs), policy or rules engines, workflow orchestration, state machines, data-lifecycle systems, or audit architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferred experience with privacy, consent, data governance, or regulatory systems, including concepts such as the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA), data-subject rights, retention, deletion, and legal holds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to translate ambiguous legal, policy, and product requirements into clear platform boundaries, reusable abstractions, and executable roadmaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense and the ability to partner effectively with Legal, Product, Design, Security, Data, Marketing, Support, and engineering teams across multiple brands and geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A growth mindset—you are eager to expand your skills, raise the quality bar, and build enduring systems in a rapidly changing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
