&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior DevSecOps&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;: London | Practice Area: Technology &amp;amp; Engineering | Type: Permanent&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build the platforms that power secure, intelligent and scalable enterprise engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Capco, we&#39;re looking for a Senior DevSecOps Engineer to help design, build and modernise enterprise software delivery capabilities for leading financial services organisations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll play a key role in developing a modern enterprise Software Development Lifecycle (SDLC) platform, with a focus on CI/CD automation, policy-as-code, security controls and cloud-native engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on engineering opportunity where you&#39;ll translate architecture into production-ready capabilities, integrate complex enterprise technologies and support engineering teams in adopting scalable, secure delivery practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll also explore approved AI-enabled engineering tools and workflows to improve development productivity, automation and delivery quality, while maintaining appropriate human oversight, security controls and responsible AI practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build modern CI/CD platforms: Design, develop and implement enterprise GitLab SaaS CI/CD pipelines, reusable engineering patterns and automated workflows, leveraging approved AI-assisted engineering capabilities where appropriate to improve efficiency and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed security and governance: Implement policy-as-code, automated security and quality gates, change controls, SAST, DAST, secrets management and vulnerability management throughout the SDLC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineer cloud-native solutions: Build and integrate services across Azure, Kubernetes and Azure API Management, supporting application, cloud and data workloads, including Snowflake and Salesforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modernise enterprise engineering environments: Support migrations from legacy Jenkins, GitLab, SonarQube, Artifactory/Nexus and AWS environments, integrating observability capabilities using Grafana and Prometheus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable engineering teams: Translate target architecture into working production capabilities, develop reusable platform services and onboard engineering teams, promoting responsible AI-enabled workflows with appropriate review, auditability and human decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GitLab and Azure expertise: Extensive hands-on experience designing, building and operating enterprise GitLab CI/CD pipelines and Azure-based engineering solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud-native engineering: Strong practical experience with Kubernetes, DevSecOps principles, infrastructure automation and policy-as-code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security and governance integration: Experience embedding identity, security controls, automated testing, quality gates and compliance requirements into enterprise delivery pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise modernisation: Demonstrated experience modernising complex engineering environments, integrating multiple technologies and delivering scalable, production-ready platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical leadership and delivery: Ability to take architectural designs through implementation, collaborate with engineering teams and support knowledge transfer, with an interest in applying approved AI tools and automation responsibly to improve engineering outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating Azure API Management with cloud-native platforms and enterprise applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Snowflake, Salesforce and engineering patterns supporting data-intensive workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience migrating from Jenkins, SonarQube, Artifactory/Nexus or AWS-based engineering environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Grafana, Prometheus and enterprise observability practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI-assisted development tools or AI-enabled DevSecOps workflows, with an understanding of responsible AI, human review and appropriate security guardrails.&lt;/li&gt;
